    t: "7 Your own local database, step by step Copy the shared dev database onto your laptop once, then every job, log, and row is yours. Done for the first time on 2026-09-09/10; about 30 minutes. Tools. Docker Desktop running, brew install supabase/tap/supabase, Postgres client tools 16+. Node 22 or 23 from nvm for the apps. Start local Supabase from the repo root. Migrations and seed are off in supabase/config.toml because we restore a real copy instead of replaying 937 files. supabase start -x edge-runtime,logflare,vector,imgproxy Database on 54322, API on 54321, console on 54323. Keys are the standard local ones printed by supabase status. Vector extension in public. The dev database has it there, and the dump types columns as public.vector. Putting it under extensions makes 15 tables fail. psql postgresql://postgres:postgres@127.0.0.1:54322/postgres -c \"create extension vector with schema public; create extension pg_trgm with schema extensions;\" Dump the dev database in pgAdmin: format Custom, whole database is fine. The file is made by Postgres 17 tools, so restore with the tools inside the container. Restore, auth first then public, because profile rows point at auth users: docker cp ~/backup.dump supabase_db_roas-local:/tmp/backup.dump docker exec supabase_db_roas-local pg_restore --data-only --no-owner -n auth -t users -t identities -d postgresql://postgres:postgres@127.0.0.1:5432/postgres /tmp/backup.dump docker exec supabase_db_roas-local pg_restore --no-owner -n public -d postgresql://postgres:postgres@127.0.0.1:5432/postgres /tmp/backup.dump If identities fail on a foreign key, run the identities line again after users landed. Expect zero errors on the public restore. Turn off cloud routing on your profile, or the api sends your jobs to a cloud runtime: update profiles set agent_runtime_type='fly_machine', agent_runtime_url=null where id='<your user id>'; Point the apps at it. In apps/api/.env: SUPABASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:54321, the local anon key, service role key, and JWT secret; REDIS_URL=redis://localhost:6379; PORT=3001. In apps/web/.env.local: the two NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_* values. Create apps/agent-api/.env with PORT=3003 so it stops borrowing the api's port. Restart api, web, agent-api. Log in again with the same password; it carried over. Run the textbook import test to prove it. 📍 Env loading: api apps/api/src/app.module.ts:80-82 (its own .env then apps/mission-worker/.env); agent-api apps/agent-api/src/lib/agent-api-env.ts:5-8 (own .env, then ../api/.env) · runtime routing apps/api/src/modules/user-agent-api/services/user-agent-api.service.ts:78-118 · profile columns profiles.agent_runtime_type, profiles.agent_runtime_url ⚠️ Known gaps: Supabase storage buckets are not restored, so transcript uploads log \"Bucket not found\" and the Train Brain file tab needs a bucket; find_connections_between is missing in dev too, so brain stats fail here as well.",
