    t: '4 Import a past meeting by hand The point. The Brain training panel lists your recent Fathom meetings and Fireflies transcripts; pick one and it is imported into the brain you chose. Read AI has no list because Read AI only pushes reports; its meetings arrive on their own. SituationSara opens Train on an agent brain, picks a Fireflies transcript from last week, and presses "Add 1 to queue". What happensThe panel asked the API which note takers exist and which are connected, so only connected ones are offered. The import call names the tool and the meeting id; the API asks that tool\'s plug-in to fetch the transcript, checks Sara may write to that brain and has credits, and queues the same "meeting transcript import" job the webhook path uses. What you seeOne job in the tray, then the meeting\'s memories on the agent\'s graph. 📍 Screen: Train modal web/features/brain/components/training/TrainingModal.tsx:34 · which tools show web/features/brain/components/training/use-training-modal-integrations.ts:68 · queue dispatch web/features/brain/components/training/training-queue-dispatch.ts:127 Fathom, :134 Fireflies 📍 Calls: web/lib/brain/brain-import-api.ts:286 listMeetingProviders → GET /integrations/meetings/providers api/meetings/intake/controllers/meeting-imports.controller.ts:38 · import brain-import-api.ts:87 and :111 → POST /integrations/meetings/:provider/import :50 → api/meetings/intake/services/meeting-import.service.ts:25 · lists GET /integrations/fathom/meetings fathom-meetings.controller.ts:46, GET /integrations/fireflies/transcripts fireflies.controller.ts:84 The panel still shows Fathom and Fireflies as two source kinds (web/features/brain/components/training/types.ts:13); a single "Meetings" source fed by the providers list is a logged follow-up. The Fireflies "Sync" button (fireflies.controller.ts:126) queues the last twenty transcripts through the same import service.',
