    tab: 'Evidence',
    t: '4 The failure modes this test catches Fast fake success. Ingest returns OK in under 500 ms, no new source, job result says "already present". Cause: a leftover fingerprint in ns_content_hashes for this brain. The fingerprint is registered before the work, so one crashed attempt poisons all retries. Clear with delete from ns_content_hashes where brain_id=\'…\', then re-arm. See Brain, Live finding 3. Silent laptop. Job goes to processing and succeeds or retries, but no local log line appears. Cause: another api on the same database took it. See Live finding 2. Source stuck at processing, zero entries. The ingest crashed after creating the source. The reason is in the agent-api log as a line starting "Failed to". No code marks the source failed. Wrong process on a port. agent-api has no env file of its own and borrows the api\'s, including PORT. If apps/api/.env says 3001, a freshly started agent-api tries 3001 too. Give agent-api its own apps/agent-api/.env with PORT=3003. "Bucket not found" after every Atlas run is the transcript upload to Supabase storage, which a restored local database does not have. Harmless for this test. 📍 Early exit: agent-brain/services/sk-ingestion.service.ts:66-73 (registerForBrain then return duplicate) before createSkSource at :81 · fingerprint: agent-brain/services/content-dedupe.service.ts:37-52 · env borrowing: apps/agent-api/src/lib/agent-api-env.ts:5-8 · transcript upload: agent-api SessionsStorageService',
