    t: '2 The one workflow every change goes through Use this order for any change, small or big. It matches the order the shipping command uses, so nothing is surprised at pull-request time. Say how you will know it worked, before coding. One line per acceptance rule: the route or command, the expected state, and the exact evidence. "Loads without error" is not evidence; "GET /api/brain/health returns 200 with memory_count > 0" is. Write or update the unit test next to the code. Same folder, .test.ts suffix. Fake the database like the existing tests do. Run the tests for that app only. pnpm --filter <app> test <path>. Red first if it is a bug fix, then green. Run type check and lint for that app. Web lint has known old violations on main; only new ones count. If a route changed, run the integration test for it, or add one in apps/api/src/test/integration/. If a screen changed, look at it. Start the app yourself, then run the browser tests or the visual check at phone, tablet, and desktop widths. Never let a test start a server. If it touches queues or outside services, run the matching smoke script against your local stack, never against staging or production with side effects. Write the doc and changelog, then commit. The commit hook runs the size check and linter on the staged files. Then open the pull request. 📍 Acceptance rule wording from .claude/rules/testing.md · order from .claude/rules/git-workflow.md "Ship order is docs → tests → review → remediate → approve → commit → push → PR" · known lint baseline noted in AGENTS.md "Cursor Cloud specific instructions" SituationWing fixes the Slack end-date bug from the Brain page, Problem 2, cause 2a. What happensWing writes the acceptance rule first: "a personal Slack import for 1 to 7 September never includes a message stamped 8 September". Then adds a test in the brain tests folder that fakes Slack returning messages on both sides of the end date and expects only the in-range ones. Runs the brain tests, sees red, fixes the input builder to pass the end date, sees green. Runs api type check and lint. No screen changed, so no browser test. Writes the changelog line, commits, and the hook passes. What you seeOne new test file, one green run, one pull request with the acceptance rule in its description. 📍 Bug: apps/api/src/modules/brain/services/brain-import-jobs-input.base.ts:277 · existing Slack tests to copy from: apps/api/src/modules/brain/services/__tests__/brain-import-jobs-slack-person.test.ts, brain-import-sweep-schedule.test.ts · pull request template .github/pull_request_template.md',
