    tab: 'Overview',
    t: '3 The seven doors, one story each ✍️ Typed or pasted text SituationSara pastes her positioning statement into "Remember this". What happensThe API checks the text is not empty and the source is one of document, Dropbox, or Google Drive. A job of type document-remember is queued with a fingerprint of the text so the same paste is not queued twice while running. Atlas reads it and saves the durable parts. What you seeA job in the import tray that turns green, then new memories in her personal brain. 📍 Code: brain/controllers/memories.controller.ts:39 POST /api/brain/remember → brain/services/brain-import-jobs-enqueue.base.ts:10 enqueueDocumentRemember 🗄️ Table: brain_import_jobs (job_type=document_remember) 📄 Uploaded file SituationOmar drops a PDF brochure and a PowerPoint deck. What happensThe API first turns the file into text: PDFs by reading their text and falling back to Gemini reading the pages as images, Word files with a converter, decks and images always by Gemini image reading. The text then goes through the same remember path as typed text. What you seeExtracted text preview, then a queued job, then memories. Scanned PDFs with no text still work because of the image fallback. 📍 Code: brain/controllers/sk.controller.ts POST /api/brain/sk/extract-text → brain/services/document-extraction.service.ts:13 extractText → brain/services/gemini-ocr.service.ts; then brain/controllers/import-jobs.controller.ts:28 POST /api/brain/import-jobs/remember-document 🔗 Link SituationSara pastes a YouTube link to a competitor\'s webinar. What happensA link-import job is queued with a fingerprint of the URL. The worker fetches the page. For YouTube it pulls the transcript; for a web page it strips the HTML down to text; for an image URL it asks Gemini to read it. That text goes to Atlas. What you seeMemories with the video\'s title as their source. 📍 Code: brain/controllers/memories.controller.ts:91 POST /api/brain/remember-link → brain/services/brain-import-jobs-enqueue.base.ts:51 enqueueUserLinkImport → brain/services/link-extraction.service.ts:17 extract 🎙️ Note taker meeting (Fathom, Fireflies, Read AI, defined tools) SituationA recorded discovery call finishes in Fathom, Fireflies or Read AI, or in a note taker a platform admin defined from Settings › Integrations › More integrations. What happensSince ROA-40 (2026-09-15) every note taker knocks on the same door: the tool posts its report to the address ROAS gave the user at connect time, the provider adapter checks the signature, and one intake service does the rest. It records the delivery (so a repeated webhook is ignored), checks the connection\'s auto-ingest switch, fetches the transcript when the tool only sent a pointer (Fireflies), normalises the report into one meeting shape, queues one meeting transcript import ticket for Atlas, and routes the call into the Meetings space. A campaign target turns the ticket into a campaign meeting import instead. Fireflies can also be pulled by hand from the Recurring tab; Read AI and defined tools only push. What you seeA row on the Activity tab named after the meeting, memories with the meeting title as source (or a "skipped" result when the transcript held nothing durable), the call in the Meetings space, and possibly a cross-brain suggestion offering to copy the memories into a related campaign. 📍 Code: shared door apps/api/src/modules/meetings/intake/controllers/meeting-webhooks.controller.ts:14 POST /api/integrations/meetings/webhooks/:provider/:connectionKey → apps/api/src/modules/meetings/intake/services/meeting-intake.service.ts (delivery claim :109, auto-ingest gate :164, ticket :223 enqueueBrainImport → enqueueMeetingTranscriptImport, Meetings space :191) · adapters apps/api/src/modules/meetings/providers/{fathom,fireflies,read-ai}-meeting-source.ts, defined tools apps/api/src/modules/meetings/custom/ · registry apps/api/src/modules/meetings/providers/meeting-provider.registry.ts · the old Fathom-only door apps/api/src/modules/integrations/fathom/controllers/fathom-webhooks.controller.ts:34 stays registered until webhooks are re-registered (ROA-40 follow-up) · suggestions brain/services/brain-cross-pollinator.service.ts · 🗄️ meeting_webhook_deliveries, meeting_provider_definitions, brain_import_jobs. Full story: Integrations › Meeting note takers. 💬 Slack channel SituationThe "#acme-client" channel is mapped to the Acme campaign brain with a weekly schedule. What happensA scheduler outside this folder queues a Slack-period job for the week. The worker pulls the channel\'s threads for that period, labels each message with who sent it and their role, and gives the bundle to Atlas with the instruction to keep only decisions, direction, customer insight, learning, and commitments. Messages from friends and family are skipped. Some senders can trigger a second copy into the customer brain or their own brain. What you seeA handful of memories per week, not every message. See Problem 2 for what can go wrong. 📍 Code: brain/services/brain-import-jobs-enqueue.base.ts:267 enqueueSlackPeriodImport → brain/services/brain-import-jobs-input.base.ts:217 buildSlackMissionInput → Atlas rule brain/services/brain-import-jobs-execution.base.ts:256 🗄️ Table: slack_brain_mappings in migrations/20260508140700_slack_brain_mappings.sql:8 🗂️ ROAS Portal (Page Grader) Two names, one system. "The ROAS Portal" is what users see on screen; "Page Grader" is the name in the code and the routes. It is a separate ROAS product that holds client accounts, pipeline stages, tasks, and client intel, connected from Workspace Settings › Integrations with its base URL and an API key. It does not scan websites; it exports a package of what it already knows. SituationAn operator maps Portal client "Acme Dental" to ROAS, or the Portal pushes an update. What happensThe API receives the client package, finds or creates the campaign and its spaces, syncs offers and avatars, then runs a deterministic ingest with no Atlas: it builds memory rows from the profile, offers, avatars, strategies, and notes, skips work if the package did not change, fills in missing fingerprints, and writes evidence chunks for search. It records a green job row so the tray shows it. What you seeA campaign, spaces with a Campaign Brief, and a brain full of Acme facts. Re-imports of an unchanged package are quick. 📍 Code: brain/controllers/page-grader-client-import.controller.ts:24 POST /api/brain/page-grader/client-package → brain/services/page-grader-client-import.service.ts:52 importPackage → brain/services/page-grader-brain-package-ingest.service.ts:42 ingestPackage 🗄️ Tables: ns_memories · ns_brain_evidence_chunks in migrations/20260525110600_brain_evidence_chunks.sql:4 · brain_import_jobs (page_grader_brain_sync) 🗨️ Chat with the helper SituationSara has a long chat with the helper about next quarter\'s offer. What happensThe conversation is sent for processing. Gemini is asked to pull out only things that "would still matter in 6 months". Items scoring under 0.6 are dropped. Each survivor gets a fingerprint, is checked against existing memories by hash, and saved. In the background, similar memories get linked and each memory is tagged with its emotion. The session is recorded so the same chat is not processed twice. What you seeA few memories, sometimes with "supports" or "contradicts" links to older ones. 📍 Two different roads. A "remember this" said to the helper in chat goes through agent-api, not this folder: the helper must call the save_user_memory action → apps/agent-api/src/modules/artifacts/services/artifact-legacy-team-brain-memory.service.ts:11 saveMemory → one row in ns_memories under the user\'s default brain. A whole conversation processed afterwards uses this folder: brain/controllers/memories.controller.ts:114 POST /api/brain/process/conversation → brain/services/conversation-processing.service.ts:52 processConversation 🗄️ Tables: ns_memories · ns_memory_connections migrations/047_brain_consolidation.sql:64 · ns_memory_sessions :83',
