    p: 'system-map/brain.html',
    pt: 'Brain',
    id: 'tables',
    h: 'Where it is stored',
    tab: 'Overview',
    t: '4 Where it is stored Everything hangs off the brains table. Colors show what each group of tables is for. Most tables were created in one migration, migrations/047_brain_consolidation.sql; the line number after each name points there unless another file is given. 🧭 Are these separate things or stages of one flow? Separate tables. See the shelves, one by one in the Flow tab. 📓 Core notebook ns_brains :8ns_memories :29ns_memory_connections :64ns_memory_versions :97ns_memory_sessions :83ns_snapshots :112ns_snapshot_edges :152ns_content_hashes :420ns_pending_captures :357 📚 Agent textbook (SK) ns_sk_sources :239ns_sk_entries :263ns_sk_gaps :296 🧭 Thinking layer ns_emotional_responses :174ns_belief_patterns :196ns_perspectives :219ns_narrative_pagesns_narrative_linksbrain_timelinesbrain_timeline_itemsbrain_episodesns_brain_evidence_chunks 🗄️ narrative pages and links migrations/20260406130000_brain_narrative_pages.sql · timelines migrations/20260618143000_brain_timelines.sql · episodes and final shapes migrations/20260618163348_brain_temporal_runtime_repair.sql · evidence chunks migrations/20260525110600_brain_evidence_chunks.sql:4 What fills these tables: Cortex Max. In one line: it keeps a brain thinking in the background, turning many memories into pages, timelines, and belief patterns, so the helper can answer about the big picture and how it changed over time. Crystallize, by contrast, goes deep on one text and writes one snapshot. A per-brain switch (ns_brains.cortex_max). Off, the brain only stores what you feed it. On, background jobs write narrative pages (the "library"), timelines, belief patterns and perspectives, and refreshed customer avatars. Switching it on queues a first full library sync; then every 10 new memories queues a library sync, every 5 changed pages a pattern analysis, and new customer memories an avatar pass. "Crystallize" forces a full rebuild. Jobs go through the brain-ops outbox and need a worker; on the local stack they never finish (see Issues). 📍 switch brain/services/brain-cortex-max.service.ts:80-93 · triggers brain/services/brain-ops-hook.service.ts:102-116,205-215,260-272 · job kinds brain_library_sync, brain_pattern_analysis, brain_timeline_synthesis, brain_avatar_synthesis · 🗄️ brain_ops_outbox migrations/20260407100000_brain_ops_outbox.sql · user side Features › Brain § 10 📋 Jobs and plumbing brain_import_jobsbrain_ops_outboxbrain_sharesbrain_cross_suggestionsslack_brain_mappingsuser_notificationsns_search_feedback :435 🗄️ migrations/20260303120000_brain_import_jobs.sql:1 · migrations/20260407100000_brain_ops_outbox.sql · migrations/20260520210300_brain_access_control.sql · migrations/20260424210000_brain_cross_suggestions.sql · migrations/20260508140700_slack_brain_mappings.sql:8 · user_notifications only in scripts/roas/roas-drift-recovery.sql:41 🏢 Company brain company_cortex_settingscompany_cortex_signalscompany_cortex_objectscompany_cortex_object_edgesdream_ops_settings 🗄️ migrations/20260518115500_company_cortex_foundation.sql:24 · migrations/20260518124000_company_cortex_objects.sql:1 · migrations/20260519140500_company_cortex_object_edges.sql · migrations/20260624203000_shared_dream_ops.sql 🧑‍🤝‍🧑 Customer and campaign customer_entitiescustomer_source_identitiescustomer_avatarscontactscampaign_nodescampaignsspacesspace_itemsoffersavatars 🗄️ migrations/20260624110423_customer_brain_identity_graph.sql · migrations/20260507142000_customer_brain_infra.sql · migrations/048_campaign_knowledge_graph.sql:6 · campaigns, contacts, offers, avatars from the pre-migration supabase/schema.sql · spaces from migrations/20260413100000_lists_mvp.sql renamed in migrations/20260422120000_spaces_rename_and_schema.sql Access control. SQL function can_access_brain(brain_id, level) at migrations/20260520210300_brain_access_control.sql:80 is the single row-level-security gate: owner → org role → agent creator → brain_shares (user, org, team). The API mirrors it in brain/services/brain-permissions.service.ts. Vectors. All embeddings are vector(768), cosine. hnsw on memories (047:58), sk_entries (047:290), evidence chunks, beliefs, perspectives, narrative pages, customer avatars, signals, timeline items (migrations/20260525221500_brain_complete_retrieval_lanes.sql). ivfflat on campaign_nodes and company_cortex_objects. No index at all on ns_snapshots.embedding.',
