    t: '8 The shelves: separate tables, not stages of one flow Short answer. Memories, SK entries, snapshots, beliefs, perspectives, pages, and timelines are different tables. A memory never turns into a snapshot. An SK entry never turns into a memory. The words fact, decision, insight, story, framework, preference, event are labels inside the memories table, not shelves of their own. SituationSara sees a memory "we price at $99 because of support cost" and a snapshot "Premium positioning principle" and asks whether one grew into the other. What happensNo. The memory came from the document pipeline. The snapshot came from crystallize, which takes raw text and writes a fresh snapshot row; it never reads the memories table. Two shelves, two searches, same idea twice. What you seeBoth show up in search under different lanes: "memories" and "snapshots". 📍 brain/services/crystallization.service.ts:66,185 takes input: string · document pipeline brain/services/document-ingestion.service.ts:155 ShelfOne row isTable, migrationFilled byRead by 📓 MemoriesOne distilled sentence, with a type label, a score, a hash, and 768 numbers.ns_memories, migrations/047_brain_consolidation.sql:29Atlas via save_user_memory; document, chat, customer, and Page Grader pipelinessearch_ns_memories at 047:529 🔗 Memory links"Supports" or "contradicts" between two memories.ns_memory_connections, 047:64brain/repositories/memories.repository.ts:241brain/repositories/brain-retrieval.repository.ts:219 📚 SK textbookA source (book, PDF, transcript) and its entries (one concept or technique each).ns_sk_sources 047:239, ns_sk_entries 047:263Atlas via ingest_agent_brain_text → sk-ingestion.service.ts:144search_sk_entries at 047:623 💎 SnapshotsOne crystallized belief: claim, story, emotion, method, stress test. Richer than a memory.ns_snapshots, 047:112brain/services/crystallization.service.ts:185; accepted captures brain/repositories/pending-captures.repository.ts:31find_similar_snapshots at 047:561 🧾 Evidence chunksA raw slice of the original text, kept so answers can quote it.ns_brain_evidence_chunks, migrations/20260525110600_brain_evidence_chunks.sql:4side-car of crystallize :189 and SK ingest :110search_brain_evidence_chunks 🔢 Fingerprints"This exact text was already ingested into this brain."ns_content_hashes, 047:420brain/repositories/content-dedupe.repository.ts:49the fingerprint gate, step 16 🧠 Belief patternsA recurring belief spotted across many memories. Keyed by person, not by brain.ns_belief_patterns, 047:196brain/repositories/emotional-intelligence.repository.ts:100; Atlas cognition toolssearch_ns_belief_patterns 🪟 PerspectivesA worldview made of several beliefs.ns_perspectives, 047:219apps/agent-api/src/modules/artifacts/repositories/artifact-brain-cognition.repository.ts:128search_ns_perspectives 📄 Narrative pagesA wiki-style page Atlas writes from many memories.ns_narrative_pages, migrations/20260406130000_brain_narrative_pages.sql:8apps/agent-api/src/modules/artifacts/repositories/artifact-brain-narrative.repository.ts:149search_narrative_pages 📅 TimelinesA dated line of events about one subject.brain_timelines migrations/20260618143000_brain_timelines.sql:7, items :40artifact-brain-narrative.repository.ts:101,128search_brain_timeline_items 📥 Pending capturesProposed snapshots from the extension, waiting for a yes.ns_pending_captures, 047:357brain/repositories/pending-captures.repository.ts:8the review screen 🎫 Import ticketsOne job. Not knowledge, a work ticket.brain_import_jobs, migrations/20260303120000_brain_import_jobs.sql:1stage 1the import tray How the shelves feed each other Doors fill three shelves directly: Memories, SK textbook, Snapshots. Pending captures become Snapshots only after a person accepts. Side-cars written at the same moment: Evidence chunks (raw text) and Fingerprints. Built later, from many rows: Memories → Belief patterns → Perspectives; Memories → Narrative pages; Memories and episodes → Timelines. Never: Memory → Snapshot. SK entry → Memory. The only SK copy-out goes to the campaign graph on hand-off. 📍 ns_belief_patterns.supporting_memories 047:202 · ns_perspectives.beliefs 047:224 · ns_narrative_pages.source_refs · hand-off copy brain/services/brain-handoff.service.ts:172-186 The seven memory labels Every memory row carries one of these in memory_type. Gemini picks the label while extracting. preference: a belief, value, or opinion. decision: a choice, with its reasoning. story: an experience that shaped thinking. framework: a repeatable method or model. insight: a non-obvious lesson. fact: a milestone or data point that matters. event: a specific occurrence. 📍 type list apps/api/src/modules/brain/types/brain.types.ts:5-12 · meanings in the extractor prompt brain/services/document-ingestion.service.ts:348-354 · 🗄️ the column is free text with no check, 047:34. See Other finding 6.',
