    h: 'Introduction',
    tab: 'Overview',
    t: "🎙️ Meeting note takers: Fathom, Fireflies, Read.ai Last updated: 2026-09-14 Category: Integrations Linear: ROA-40 · ROA-44 Source of truth: apps/api/src/modules/integrations/{fathom,fireflies,read-ai}, apps/api/src/modules/meetings, .docs/plans/meeting-notetaker-system-roa-40.md User's side: Features › Meeting note takers How meeting recordings get from an AI note taker into ROAS, the three problems the old code had, and the modular system (ROA-40) that replaced them. Phases 0 to 4 are built, tested and pushed on branch claude/roa-40-modular-meeting-system; Phase 5, the live run with real accounts, is in review. Section 1 keeps the old pipes for the record; sections 3 to 6 describe what is built now. For the screens and what you can do, read Features › Meeting note takers. 📍 Paths starting with fathom/ mean apps/api/src/modules/integrations/fathom/, fireflies/ means apps/api/src/modules/integrations/fireflies/, meetings/ means apps/api/src/modules/meetings/, brain/ means apps/api/src/modules/brain/, web/ means apps/web/src/. The API adds /api in front of every route. In one paragraph Before ROA-40, two note takers were connected through two separate pipes: Fathom deep (recording lands in the brain, the Meetings space and the customer and campaign brains), Fireflies shallow (a brain job that never carried the transcript). Now there is one shared definition of a meeting, one front door every tool posts to, one brain import job, and Fathom, Fireflies and Read.ai are plug-ins behind it. The three problems below are fixed. What remains is the live run (Phase 5) and two production chores: apply the two migrations and run the Fathom re-registration script, after which the old Fathom door can go.",
