    t: "7 Findings and evidence Provider facts verified from official docs (2026-09-11) ProviderHow we get the meetingSignatureLoginSource FathomPush; transcript and summary may need a fetch (/recordings/{id}/transcript, 30 calls per minute)webhook-id, webhook-timestamp, webhook-signature; HMAC-SHA256 over id.timestamp.body; secret after whsec_, base64; 5-minute windowOAuth 2.0; we register the webhook with destination_url and triggered_fordevelopers.fathom.ai/webhooks FirefliesPush ping { meetingId, eventType } then GraphQL transcript(id) fetchx-hub-signature, HMAC-SHA256 with a user-set 16 to 32 character secret (encoding to be confirmed)API key, Authorization: Bearer; user pastes our URL in Developer settingsdocs.fireflies.ai Read.aiPush; full report in the body (transcript.speaker_blocks, summary, action_items, participants, report_url, request_id)X-Read-Signature, hex HMAC-SHA256 of the raw body with the base64-decoded signing keySigning key pasted by the user; Pro or Enterprise plan; up to 20 webhooks per usersupport.read.ai Hardcoded lists a provider must join today These were why \"add a provider\" was a ten-file change. Status 2026-09-14: the API-side lists now include read_ai and the training panel reads the registry through GET /integrations/meetings/providers; the web lists still name each provider (single \"Meetings\" source in the training panel is a logged follow-up). apps/api/src/modules/integrations/services/integrations-overview.service.ts:17 INTEGRATION_IDS_FOR_OVERVIEW apps/api/src/modules/integrations/services/personal-cross-context-providers.ts:11 PERSONAL_CROSS_CONTEXT_PROVIDERS apps/api/src/modules/integrations/services/integrations-composio.service.ts:48 PERSONAL_ONLY brain/types/brain.types.ts:21 SourceType · brain/repositories/brain-import-job-status.repository.ts:54 job-type lists · brain/repositories/memory-stats.repository.ts:392 web/lib/integrations/integration-catalog.ts:406, integration-logo.ts:28, web/features/settings/components/settings-content/integration-connection-label.ts:55, useIntegrations.ts:513 and :657 (872-line file, hook limit 300) web/features/brain/components/training/types.ts:13, use-training-modal-integrations.ts:72, training-queue-dispatch.ts:127 packages/api-shared/src/types/customer-interaction.ts:9 INTERACTION_CHANNELS Meetings-space coupling apps/api/src/modules/spaces/services/space-automation-service-06.base.ts:294 processFathomRecordingEvent reads a Fathom-shaped body and claims space_external_automation_events with provider 'fathom'; the provider CHECK is ('gmail','outlook','fathom') in supabase/migrations/20260510091200_space_external_automation_fathom.sql:16. The Flow trigger external_fathom_recording_ready has 63 references, so the plan keeps its name and adds a provider field; the rename is a logged follow-up. Open questions, now for the Phase 5 live run Fireflies signature encoding (hex or base64, sha256= prefix): capture one real delivery on a test account. Fireflies and Read.ai retry behaviour: return one 500 during the test and watch redelivery. Read.ai REST API login: not needed; Read AI ships as push-only with no past-meetings list. Does Fathom accept a destination_url with a path segment for the connection key. Where an MCP-backed fetch runs: apps/agent-api/src/modules/mcp/ has the client; apps/api does not.",
