    tab: 'Overview',
    t: '? Questions people asked Will the structure support any other system, not just the listed note takers? 2026-09-12 Yes for anything that delivers a transcript as text. The contract fixes only the shape of the result; how it arrives (push, poll, user click, agent action) and how you log in (OAuth, API key, signing key, MCP) are the plug-in\'s choice. Audio without text needs a transcription step first; that is a separate feature the contract leaves room for. 📍 .docs/plans/meeting-notetaker-system-roa-40.md "Extensibility Model" Would it support an MCP connection? 2026-09-12 Yes, as a pull transport. An MCP server never calls us, so an MCP-backed tool joins through the scheduled poll, a user click, or the agent action; its plug-in implements the pull group with an MCP session instead of REST. Open question: whether that client runs in api or agent-api. 📍 apps/agent-api/src/modules/mcp/repositories/mcp.repository.ts Where is testing in the delivery? 2026-09-12 Every phase has its own proof (section 6), and Phase 5 is a full-flow run with a real meeting recorded by all three tools, checked across Settings, Meetings space, brain, training panel, Vibey chat and the Slack flow. 📍 plan "Test Plan" and "Phase 5" How this page was made: three read-only code sweeps (meeting code, integrations architecture, brain import doors) plus the official Fathom, Fireflies and Read.ai webhook docs, all re-verified in the source on 2026-09-11; written as the human view of .docs/plans/meeting-notetaker-system-roa-40.md.',
