    t: '1 Open issues AreaIssueWhy it mattersStatusLinear Brain queueTwo workers listen on the brain import queue; which one runs a job is luckThe api runs jobs in-process, the mission worker forwards them to agent-api. Both attach to the same Redis queue, so logs and behavior move between processes.open, highROA-33 Brain queueapi worker drops the hourly Page Grader catch-up sweepThe api registers the hourly timer but its worker only understands the 3-second one. With the api as the only consumer, catch-up never runs.openROA-34 Brain queue20-minute stale window can re-run a big import and pay for a chunk twiceEach Atlas chunk call can take 15 minutes; a three-chunk job legitimately passes 20. The sweep reclaims it mid-flight.openROA-35 BrainMemories created through the plain API have no embeddingThe create endpoint hashes and inserts but never embeds, so search by meaning cannot find those rows.openROA-36 BrainChat processing never fingerprints the whole conversationReplaying a conversation pays Gemini again and can insert near-duplicate memories.openROA-37 Brain / DBMemory, source, and snapshot types are not enforced by the databaseFree-text columns, code writes values outside its own list, and a snapshot default ("Belief") the code never produces.openROA-38 Agent chatHelper never reads the personal brain before answering, and is denied its memory toolsRoot cause found: the chat prewarm service declares the policy service as Type | undefined behind @Optional(), so Nest injects nothing and the personal-brain flag is always false. Explains this and Live finding 1. Two-line fix plus a DI test.fixed 2026-09-15ROA-32, blocks ROA-29 Agent chatHelper\'s search skipped textbook entries in personal and customer brainsThe Specific Knowledge lane ran only for agent brains, so trained techniques and principles in a personal brain never reached chat. Fixed: lane runs for every brain family; trained items carry provenance (type, mastery, confidence, training source).fixed 2026-09-15ROA-53 Brain / UIActivity tab shows a skipped import exactly like a successful oneWhen Atlas reads a transcript and keeps nothing (status skipped, reason stored on the job row), the row still shows a green check and a dash. Users cannot tell "saved 5 memories" from "saved nothing" without asking. Show the skip reason in the list.no ticket yet BrainBrain health counters disagreetotal_memories says 1 while memory_counts_by_type is empty after a successful save. Two queries, two answers.no ticket yet BrainCrashed textbook import poisons retries, retries report successFingerprint is registered before the work. One crash means every retry says "already present" and the job is marked succeeded with zero entries. Proven locally 2026-09-10.openno ticket yet Local devagent-api borrows the api\'s env file, including PORTA fresh agent-api start binds the api\'s port and the web app then 404s. Needs its own env file with PORT=3003.openno ticket yet Local dev / infraLocal dev shares its job queue with a cloud environmentA cloud api on the same dev Redis grabs local brain jobs and runs them in the cloud. Local terminals stay silent, source rows pile up in the shared DB, errors are invisible. Fix: local Redis for local dev.openno ticket yet BrainTextbook ingest leaves sources stuck at "processing" on failureSeen twice live: source created, entries never written, no failed state, UI shows "Retrying…" forever.openno ticket yet Brain opsBrain-ops synthesis jobs never complete locally15 "Crystallize" jobs spinning for up to 2 days with no worker and no error shown.no ticket yet Agent chatHelper says "remembered" but saves nothingSeen live on dev 2026-09-09, twice. The helper is allowed to save memories but its generated docs never teach it the action, so it reaches for campaign and company actions whose docs and handlers disagree on field names. First try: 3 failures then a false "saved". Second try: 7 failures, honest reply, wrong advice.openROA-29, ROA-30, ROA-31 BrainThe AI agent uses a different copy of the brain search codeA fix in one copy does not reach the other. Bad answers may come from code nobody is looking at.openROA-9 BrainThe import doors let in unwanted dataPersonal Slack pulls past the end date, filtering is prompt-only, finished imports can repeat, copies duplicate rows.in progressROA-18 BrainDatabase and code disagreeA missing SQL function, a hand-made table, no generated types, an hourly job that does nothing.openROA-9 BrainSmaller findings: permissions, duplication, data qualityA few doors skip permission checks, two doors fetch any URL, several counters and labels are wrong.no ticket yet',
